    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nI was trying to copy/yank multiple paragraphs from one buffer to another,\nwhen I encountered this behavior, which is *\"the cursors stayed at the original buffer\"*\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open any file that has at least two paragraphs [buffer A].\n- Open a new buffer (split or whatever) [buffer B].\n- Place a cursor at the beginning each paragraph from buffer A.\n- Yank each paragraph.\n- Now go to buffer B to paste the paragraphs.\n- Only the primary cursor is moved, and it pastes what it yanked.\n\nThis also happens even when *follow* mode is activated via `q=`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe expected behavior is to move all cursors into the new buffer and paste \nthose paragraphs.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1929+g17f43325b1\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nArch Linux x86_64\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nfoot 1.28.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nfoot\n\n### Installation\n\nAUR",
